  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The Government of Republic of Zimbabwe successfully submitted the following reports under Article 22 regular reporting: 
a.2020: C14, C19, C026, C029, C081, C099, C105, C129, C138, C150, C155, C161, C162, C170, C174, C176 &amp; C182.
b.2021: C26, C99, C100, &amp; C111
2. The Government of Republic of Zimbabwe successfully submitted the following reports under Article 19 reporting: 
a. 2020: C149, C189, R157 &amp; R201 The ILO facilitated the sharing and discussion of the relevant texts including the reporting schedule with the tripartite partners; and the subsequent submission of the reports.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.1. Percentage of reports on the application of ratified Conventions due by 1 September received in a timely manner that include replies to comments of the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
