     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In October 2021, the Government of Republic of Zimbabwe successfully submitted its report to the Committee of Experts on the Applications of Conventions and Recommendations on C087 and C105 following the conclusions of the June 2021 Committee on the Application of Standards (CAS).
The same month, the Government of Zimbabwe&apos;s CABINET approved the Labour Amendment Bill 
a.	The Amendment Bill will repeal among other amendments sections 104(2)&#x2013;(3) and 109(1)&#x2013;(2) of the Labour Act (Chapter 28.01) in line with the comments made by the CEACR. 
b.	The Tripartite Negotiating Forum (TNF) Technical Committee in its meeting of October 2020 agreed and passed that the Draft Bill be submitted to CABINET
 In early October 2021, the ILO facilitated a tripartite consultative meeting to discuss and validate the draft reports by the Government of Zimbabwe.
a.	 The meeting was attended by the leadership of the Zimbabwe Congress of Trade Unions (ZCTU)-( President and Secretary General); the Zimbabwe Federation of Trade Unions(ZFTU)-(Secretary General); the Employers&apos; Confederation of Zimbabwe(EMCOZ)-(Executive Director) and representatives of government- from the Ministry of Public Service, Labour and Social Welfare, the Attorney General&apos;s Office and the Police Service.
b.	The ILO provided technical support in the meeting on the substance of the comments of the ILO Supervisory Bodies on C087 and C105 and international labour standards issues in general.   

The ILO also supported the drafting of the layman&apos;s bill and the tripartite consultations in a workshop during the 2018/19 biennium. In 2020, the ILO provided material support to the Ministry of Public Service, Labour and Social Welfare to submit the Bill to the CABINET Committee on Legislation (CCL).</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.2 Number of member States with tripartite mechanisms enabling constituents to effectively engage in the implementation of international labour standards at the national level, including reporting to the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
